Fix: give the page a hero one step above the card hero

The critique's hierarchy finding (§5) was that every number on a product
screen carries the same weight: four tiles of identical size, no figure
that commands the page. Four of its six ranked items are closed, but this
one had no token to spend — --ns-text-4xl is already the card hero, so a
page that needed a larger figure had nowhere to step.

Adds --ns-text-display (3rem) to tokens.json and tokens.css, and a card
modifier that spends it. The modifier sits on the card, not on the Hero
band, which is what widgets-card.tsx:82-86 said the fix would have to be:
the size a hero renders at is decided by where the card sits on the page,
and the card is what knows that. One card per page takes it — the runs
console's "Billed this period" and the run console's computed total, which
are the first card on their respective pages.

The gallery pairs a display card with a card hero so the step is visible,
and names the rule in its copy: two display heroes on one page is the flat
grid the step exists to avoid.
EOF
