+/**
+ * The quietest text in the product is the em dash, and it was invisible.
+ *
+ * `--ns-absent` at paper-5 measured 2.35:1 against a light card — under the
+ * 3:1 that even a large glyph needs — so every "not measured" in the product
+ * was a fact the reader could not see. The fix is measured, not eyeballed:
+ * this converts the numbers into a rule, because a tone that is only checked
+ * once drifts back the next time the paper ramp is touched.
+ *
+ * OKLCH → sRGB → WCAG relative luminance. `oklch(% C H)` is the only form the
+ * ramp uses; hex covers `--ns-card`, which is `#ffffff` in light.
